    victim_explanation = 'On July 25, 2025, the Acree family arrived at the Child Advocacy Center to be interviewed. Present for the interviews were Erin and Elizabeth Acree. The interviews were digitally recorded and will remain with the Anne Arundel County Department of Social Services investigation record. The following is a brief synopsis of events disclosed. For more detailed statements, it is recommended that authorized persons review the recorded interview in its entirety for verbatim disclosures.

The interview with Elizabeth was conducted using the ChildFirst Protocol (R-TEC) which is a semi-structured nationally recognized interview protocol. It consists of five stages (rapport building, transition to topic of concern, explore details, and closure) which can be modified or eliminated depending on the child.

Elizabeth was able to provide specific details with regards to the abuse (such as clearly stating who the alleged maltreator was, where the abuse occurred, whether clothing was on or off, whether anyone else was present, location of the alleged maltreatment, frequency, etc.).  For the complete interview, please see DVD enclosed in the case file. 

During the interview, Elizabeth stated that she told her psychiatrist that a teacher from her school was texting her and showing up at her workplace. Elizabeth stated that he isn''t even her teacher, and she found it weird. Elizabeth identified this teacher as Mr. Warrilow. She stated that he works at Chesapeake HS and he taught Junior''s, AP classes and Chemistry. Elizabeth stated that she works at an ice-cream shop, and they make snowball syrup. She stated that she has been working there for a little over a year. When asked about their relationship, she stated that the end of the school year, he was leaving for surgery, and she felt bad. Elizabeth stated that they would always talk, and he told her he liked talking to her. Elizabeth stated that when she is "tweaking out in the hallway" he always asks her to come to his classroom and get food. She stated that when she gets in her mood, she doesn''t feel like talking to anyone, and he was annoying her. Elizabeth stated that sometimes she didn''t feel like it. Elizabeth stated that at the end of the year she gave him a picture of her face that said thank you for all you''ve done for me this year and stated that she did this because she never really thanked him, she just took stuff from him. At the end of the year, he showed her his google voice number, and she added it to her phone. He also asked about Facebook, and she stated that she doesn''t use Facebook. The day before his surgery, he came to her job, and told her that the picture she gave him, "her eyes were so magical". Elizabeth stated that when he was leaving and she told him to get a heating pad, and he asked why I would get a heating pad when I have you. He also told her that he had spent $36 and gained 5 pounds coming to her job looking for her. Her co-worker also told her that he was coming there often looking for her, on days when she was not there. She also told him that she lost his number, and she was sorry she didn''t text him for the whole hospital stay. He gave her his number again. Elizabeth stated that the first time she met him in the hallways when she was taking laps, he offered her cornbread. Elizabeth stated that another time when she was walking in the hallways doing laps, he called her over to him, and pushed into her and said, "man I wish I could hug you right now", and she stated that it wasn''t appropriate. Elizabeth stated that she walked through the halls every day. Elizabeth stated that he has also bought her a sandwich from subway. Then she stated that they split it, because it was his, but he wanted her to try it. Elizabeth stated that they split it in half, and he wanted her to stay in there and eat it with him. Elizabeth stated that she stayed past the bell ringing and then she left and he told her I really enjoyed the time with you. Elizabeth stated that he has also given her oatmeal cookies because those are her favorite. He also came to her job once and gave her a chickfila gift card.  Elizabeth stated that one day she saw him with another female student with black hair, she doesn''t know her name. Mr. Warrilow told the both of them that if they ever needed to talk or needed anything, they could come to him.  Elizabeth stated that the other girl was talking about how she has anxiety, throws up all the time, and has a eating disorder. Mr. Warrilow told the girl that he has an eating disorder too, but "a different kind". Elizabeth stated that he gave her a clear capsule, and he told her that it had a diamond or crystals in it. Elizabeth stated that she threw it away because it was a pill and it was questionable. Elizabeth stated that when she saw him in the hallway, she would get annoyed because she knew he would stop her to talk to her. She stated that she was genuine with him, but it was oddly satisfying. Elizabeth stated that she still had his google voice number - 302-469-3239. She stated that they would text everyday, but it wouldn''t last long because she "wasn''t always on her phone like that". Elizabeth stated that she felt like he was pathetic, and an "old ass man", and she "doesn''t know why she fell for it".',    
